{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This structure provides a foundational framework with key architectural elements (envelope, message sections, organization roles) but is critically incomplete for D96A EANCOM INVOIC compliance. Coverage is approximately 15-20% of required segments. Missing essential segments include monetary amounts (MOA), dates (DTM), tax details (TAX), quantities (QTY), references (RFF), line item details (LIN, PIA, IMD), allowances/charges (ALC), and totals control (UNS, CNT). The model conflates abstract classes with concrete EDIFACT segments and lacks qualifier-specific semantics.",
  "completeness_score": 0.18,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Document Date (DTM+137) is MANDATORY in EANCOM INVOIC. Invoice Date (DTM+3) is also required. Missing date handling makes the model non-compliant. Must support qualifiers: 137", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 4}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "Your segment coverage is now substantially improved (~65-70% complete for D96A INVOIC), but critical gaps remain. You are missing PAC (packaging), PCD (percentage details for allowances/charges), and crucially TOD (terms of delivery) which is mandatory in many EANCOM implementations. More importantly, your model lacks the semantic differentiation layer: segments like DTM, MOA, NAD, RFF exist as generic classes, but D96A requires you to model their *qualified instances* (e.g., DTM+137 as DocumentDate, MOA+79 as TotalLineItemAmount) as distinct ontological entities with specific cardinality and validation rules.",
  "completeness_score": 0.68,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "PAC_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Packaging information (PAC) is mandatory in EANCOM INVOIC when physical goods are shipped. Without this, you cannot represent number of packages, packaging type,", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 3}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "The plan demonstrates significant progress with ~20 segment types and qualified entities. However, critical D96A INVOIC segments remain absent: CUX (Currency), FTX (Free Text), LOC (Place/Location), MEA (Measurements), and PRI (Price Details). The qualifier coverage for existing segments is incomplete—MOA lacks breakdown qualifiers (e.g., 79=Line Item Amount, 176=Message Total), and RFF needs commercial reference qualifiers (ON=Order Number, DQ=Delivery Note). Completeness score reflects ~70% segment coverage but insufficient qualifier granularity.",

  "completeness_score": 0.70,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "CUX_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Currency (CUX) is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC per EANCOM rules. Without it, multi-currency invoices cannot be validated. Must include qualifier 2 (Reference Currency) and ISO ", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 2}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "Your model now covers approximately 75-80% of a production-grade D96A EANCOM INVOIC implementation. The addition of CUX, FTX, LOC, MEA, and PRI segments, plus explicit qualified entities for critical MOA/RFF/DTM qualifiers, represents significant progress. However, critical gaps remain in allowance/charge detail modeling, party-specific tax registration, and line-level reference structures that are mandatory for retail/logistics compliance.",

  "completeness_score": 0.78,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "ALC_Detail_Group",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "ALC (Allowance/Charge) segments in D96A INVOIC require associated PCD (Percentage) and MOA (Monetary Amount) segments to specify calculation basis. Your current ALC_Segment lacks the structural relationship to its mandatory child segments. EANCOM requires ALC+A (Allowance) or ALC+C", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 1}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "The current model demonstrates strong progress with ~25 segment types and critical qualifiers defined. However, it falls short of full D96A INVOIC coverage, achieving approximately 65-70% structural completeness. Critical gaps exist in party-level tax registration (RFF+VA/FC), line-level packaging (PAC in LIN group), and multi-level allowance/charge structures. The ALC_Detail_Group is a positive addition but requires explicit cardinality constraints and hierarchical positioning.",

  "completeness_score": 0.68,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "property",
      "name": "NAD_Segment.taxRegistrationReference",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A EANCOM mandates VAT registration numbers via RFF+VA (VAT number) or RFF+FC (Fiscal number) within NAD groups. Without this, tax compliance validation is impossible. Must be modeled as a qualified RFF_Segment child of NAD, not a generic reference."", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 0}

