{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong structural foundations with proper segment class definitions and relationship modeling. However, it suffers from critical **qualifier flattening** (treating all NAD/DTM/RFF segments as homogeneous), incomplete D96A INVOIC coverage (~40% segment coverage), and missing mandatory EANCOM business rule constraints. The ontology requires substantial extension to represent a complete D96A INVOIC message.",

  "completeness_score": 0.42,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "NAD_BY_Segment (Buyer)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "CRITICAL FLATTENING ERROR: The ontology defines generic NAD_Segment but does not distinguish NAD+BY (Buyer) from NAD+SU (Supplier), NAD+DP (Delivery Party), NAD+IV (Invoicee), NAD+PE (Payee). Each qualifier creates a semantically distinct entity with different cardinality rules. In ", "owl_reviewed_length": 28778, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

