{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a reasonable high-level understanding of invoice structure (header/detail/summary) but suffers from critical EDIFACT abstraction loss. It models generic 'segments' and 'organizations' without encoding the qualifier-driven semantics that define D96A EANCOM. Coverage is approximately 15-20% of a complete INVOIC implementation.",
  "completeness_score": 0.18,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_Segment with qualifier distinctions (DTM+137, DTM+35, DTM+11)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Document Date (DTM+137) is MANDATORY in EANCOM INVOIC. The ontology has a generic 'documentDate' datatype property on HeaderSection, but lacks the segment-level representation and qualifier semantics. Without DTM+137 as a distinct class/constraint, you cannot validate that the date appears in the correct EDIFACT position with the correct qualifier."
    },", "owl_reviewed_length": 18325, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

