{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with proper reification and inverse properties, but suffers from critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC incompleteness. Coverage is approximately 20-25% of required segments. The model lacks qualifier distinctions (all NAD segments are merged), omits ~12 mandatory segment types, and contains cardinality violations. The abstract 'Segment' approach loses EDIFACT semantic precision.",
  "completeness_score": 0.23,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with qualifier subclasses (DTM+137, DTM+35, DTM+11)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A INVOIC mandates Document Date (DTM+137) as M, Delivery Date (DTM+35) as C, and Despatch Date (DTM+11) as C. The current 'documentDate' property on InvoiceHeader is insufficient - it doesn't distinguish between these semantically different dates,", "owl_reviewed_length": 16314, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

